    "question": {
      ":question/id": "78ddbb39-92a2-505c-9748-ce8332d32af4",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & -4 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 9 & -6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & -4 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 9 & -6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{2} :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9 & -6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
